WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.700
LegatorOCR turns raw book scans into a searchable PDF.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:16.700
Split, straighten, crop, clean, binarize,
then export with an OCR text layer.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:25.700
It measures the skew of the text lines
and rotates the page back.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:34.700
Mixed and hybrid modes keep sharp text
and shrink colour pages to about 60–100 KB.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:43.700
It reads scanned PDFs itself: JPEG 2000,
JBIG2, CCITT and encrypted files.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:52.700
Checked against OpenJPEG, poppler and qpdf,
and fuzzed with hostile inputs.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:01.700
One command in the terminal,
or the graphical interface in 8 languages.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:09.700
Free, local, no accounts. MIT licence.
Code on GitHub.
